# ==================== CREDENTIALS — NEVER COMMIT ====================
#
# This repo is PUBLIC (github.com/jeremypanaligan-cmd/GVSI-NETWORK-REPORT).
# Anything committed here is world-readable within minutes of a push (public
# repos are scanned by bots for exactly these patterns), and it stays readable
# in the git history even after the file itself is deleted. Removing a file is
# NOT how a leaked key is handled — the key is revoked in the provider's
# dashboard, and only then is the file removed.
#
# Apps Script sources are plain files that carry their configuration inline, so
# a key pasted into a .gs file is a key in the repo. Put secrets in
# PropertiesService.getScriptProperties() instead, and keep any file that holds
# one out of git by name.

# supabase-sync.gs held a hardcoded Supabase SECRET key (full server-side
# access, bypasses Row Level Security). File removed 2026-09-17; the entry stays
# so it cannot reappear by accident.
supabase-sync.gs

# Any future file whose name says it holds a credential.
*secret*.gs
*credentials*.gs
*-keys.gs
secrets.*
.env
.env.*
*.env

# ==================== LOCAL SCRATCH ====================
# Copied to .js for `node --check` (which rejects the .gs extension), plus
# local server output.
_chk.js
_inline_check.js
serve.log
*.log

# ==================== PYTHON ====================
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ==================== OS JUNK ====================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOTE: .vscode/launch.json and .freebuff/project-id are tracked on purpose.
# Do not add blanket rules for those directories — it would hide them from
# `git status` while they remain in the index.
